{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-06-13T07:43:20.704552911Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e5ffa6be-9e18-4820-a140-d839055050ae","comment_uuid":"eab99957-6599-46b9-ab51-146d505e63a9","author":"y4rr","content":"Correction to the 2026-06-13 closure: the verified implementation is f32-only for CUDA. Live PyTorch 2.11.0+cu130 on RTX 3090 computes torch.rand/torch.randn on CUDA for float32, float64, float16, and bfloat16. ferrotorch rand_on_device/randn_on_device currently CPU-generates then uploads for CUDA non-f32. That fallback is documented, but under the production-grade/no-shallow-GPU standard it is not a complete implementation of this broad issue title. Reopened: f32 on-device path remains verified; remaining work is true CUDA rand/randn lanes for f64/f16/bf16 or, if deliberately not implemented, a loud structured error rather than CPU generation masquerading as CUDA RNG.","created_at":"2026-06-13T07:43:20.702303360Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAEL7gSImZLotAIDK0loKj16aXFe568PZAzh0+BUkawo0RkBVpEb1JbFuyZthy2O824GMJCsPVlu6pn9S4BKPqDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNODXgVbA0HS78YAgoRukKgviCzYJ0OcY5mJZ6DpBzlTfgHHwK2ZG9heSFv/R02OJDDrR8Tq1Ef1Rl+4Fxb8VwQ="}
